ocket, especially over the past 12 months.</p>

<h2 class=3D"style-h2 mb-2 mt-4 not-prose font-normal ">Yesterday=E2=80=99s=
 API Attacks vs. today=E2=80=99s API Attacks</h2>

<hr class=3D"w-full h-[2px] text-site-hr-grey bg-site-hr-grey border-0 mt-6=
">
<p class=3D"style-p font-light ">Due to their ever-growing popularity, APIs=
 have become a key focus for cyber-attacks. In the past 12 months alone, <a=
 href=3D"https://salt.security/blog/api-security-fundamentals" class=3D"not=
-prose text-site-link active:text-site-link visited:text-site-link-visited =
font-normal hover:underline" target=3D"_blank" data-feathr-click-track=3D"t=
rue" data-feathr-link-aids=3D"5cdda43ba3a493000bf82f7f">API attack traffic =
grew by 681%</a>, with 95% of companies reporting an API security incident =
following a research report.</p>
<p class=3D"style-p font-light ">An API attack can be described as abuse or=
 illegitimate usage or attempted usage of an API for malicious intent, usua=
lly to gain illegal access to a server to exfiltrate data, or to cause serv=
ice disruption.</p>
<p class=3D"style-p font-light ">In the past, API attacks mostly relied on =
targeting known vulnerabilities, such as a SQL injection attacks, and the X=
SS attack. Today, API attacks are far more sophisticated =E2=80=93 bad acto=
rs poke and prod to learn the business logic gaps in a company=E2=80=99s AP=
Is and target those gaps.</p>

<h2 class=3D"style-h2 mb-2 mt-4 not-prose font-normal ">How do yesterday=E2=
=80=99s API Attacks work?</h2>

<hr class=3D"w-full h-[2px] text-site-hr-grey bg-site-hr-grey border-0 mt-6=
">
<p class=3D"style-p font-light ">Since APIs serve as a gateway for communic=
ation between software over the internet, they often store sensitive inform=
ation regarding implementation methods and their structure. When an attacke=
r gains access to this information, it can be used to launch cyberattacks, =
particularly ones that exploit known API vulnerabilities or improperly conf=
igured APIs. Thus, API attacks work when there is an abuse of a vulnerabili=
ty with an API, leading to unauthorized access or data leak.</p>


<hr class=3D"w-full h-[2px] text-site-hr-grey bg-site-hr-grey border-0 mt-6=
">


<p class=3D"style-p font-light "><a class=3D"not-prose text-site-link activ=
e:text-site-link visited:text-site-link-visited font-normal hover:underline=
" target=3D"_self" href=3D"https://www.computer.org/resources/newsletters/c=
omputing-edge?source=3Dtechnews" data-feathr-click-track=3D"true" data-feat=
hr-link-aids=3D"5cdda43ba3a493000bf82f7f"><span class=3D"font-medium">Want =
More Tech News? Subscribe to <i>ComputingEdge</i> Newsletter Today!</span><=
/a></p>


<hr class=3D"w-full h-[2px] text-site-hr-grey bg-site-hr-grey border-0 mt-6=
">


<h2 class=3D"style-h2 mb-2 mt-4 not-prose font-normal ">Types of known API =
vulnerabilities and how to protect against them</h2>

<hr class=3D"w-full h-[2px] text-site-hr-grey bg-site-hr-grey border-0 mt-6=
">

<ol>
